# Angular MatDialog background

In this project, global styles set `.mat-dialog-container` to **transparent** (see `frontend/src/assets/style/_global_styles.scss`). New dialogs therefore look like floating text with no card unless you style them.

## Required whenever you create or open a MatDialog

1. **Inner root element** of the dialog template must have an opaque white surface, e.g.:
   - `background: #fff;`
   - `border-radius` (e.g. 16px)
   - light border + soft box-shadow (match `promise-to-pay-dialog` / existing dialogs)
2. Pass `panelClass` (and usually `backdropClass`) on `dialog.open(...)`.
3. Register matching overlay styles in `frontend/src/styles.scss`:
   - backdrop: `rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.22)` (or project standard)
   - panel `.mat-dialog-container` / `.mat-mdc-dialog-container`: transparent, no padding/shadow (content card owns the look)

## Do not

- Rely on Material’s default white container — it is overridden globally.
- Ship a dialog whose only styles are padding/typography without `background: #fff` on the content wrapper.

## Reference

- `frontend/src/app/shared/components/promise-to-pay-dialog/`
- Overlay patterns already in `frontend/src/styles.scss` (e.g. `promise-to-pay-dialog-panel`, `admin-installment-dialog-panel`)
